what inspires me I believe it's  important that you are inspired as an  entrepreneur you're starting the  business around your passion if you  don't you're not gonna have success if  you're in it just for the money it's not  gonna work out for you I got a tweet  from one of my followers Bob Narinder  who is at Bob Narenda and he wrote in to  say so what inspires you  was there a Eureka moment that sent you  on your current path and there was so  here's what happened with my business  okay I had a software company and I  built it up I sold it when I sold it I  was kind of struggling I didn't know  what I wanted to do next you know I put  so much of myself into this business  that I needed I don't know I needed  something else to do but I didn't know  where to go and I felt like just  exploring and I tried a whole bunch of  different things and one of the ones  that came up was I talked to the YMCA a  local YMCA group and we talked about  doing a presentation where I come in and  talk about entrepreneurship young  entrepreneurs and and how to make your  dream of starting the business a reality  and they said we have this group for  entrepreneurs we have a young  entrepreneur program we'd love to have  you come and speak to them so I said  great no prob like no cost I'm just  doing this to give back and to explore  and and to help and see where it leads  and I remember I got so excited about  this I was I was making a presentation  and I I spent about a month I think  making this thing what the size were  gonna be what I was gonna talk about and  I was promoting it and the YMCA was  promoting it and about a month and  there's a free presentation and I  remember the day comes like today is a  day I'm gonna go do my presentation at  the Y you know we'll see what leads to  and my heart's pounding and I'm nervous  a little bit I hadn't done a lot of  speaking before this and I remember  getting to the door and going up the  elevator and and just getting all  excited and I go in I open the door walk  into the room when we said this huge  room up full of chairs and three people  were in the room and and I felt like  that the air was just sucked out of my  lungs like I'd spent so much time  promoting this and the YMCA promoted it  and working on the content and three  people showed up for a free event it's  like what and and it was really  heartbreaking you know I felt in that  moment like maybe I made the wrong  decision like this maybe was a stupid  thing for me to do like I had wasted a  lot of my time I hate wasting time and I  felt like this probably was a waste of  time so I continued on you know there's  three people still shut up I did this  work I need to at least deliver the  presentation and then ended up being  awesome i I went through my content and  because it was such a small group I got  to know everybody really well and got to  help them with their problems and the  challenges they faced and they laughed  as different people than when they came  in and even though it was only three  people that made me feel really good  like I knew that I had helped these  people that day and I gave them advice  that nobody else had given them before  and and I could help be the difference  between them succeeding and them not  making it with their company and that  made me feel really good and from there  I had to find the way to keep doing it  if it was presentations or websites or  videos like this or on Twitter or  Facebook or YouTube or whatever I didn't  know where would lead only that I had to  keep doing this work to help  entrepreneurs you know before I would  sound like biotech software I had  nothing to do with entrepreneurship but  I felt like after that experience I had  I had to I had to help other  entrepreneurs that was my Eureka moment  and everybody looking at that situation  might have said Evan you're kind of  crazy right like you could only get  three people to come out to a free event  that was you and the YMCA promoting it  and all three people came out like how  is this ever gonna be a business and and  I didn't have the answer like I didn't  know how I would eventually make money  from this and entrepreneurs don't have  money so how do you turn that like  logically this didn't make any sense to  get into like Evan what are you doing  this is stupid  where  with my biotech software company I'm  selling the huge companies like Knotts  and Johnson Johnson guys with huge  budgets but there was just something  about it that I loved doing and I I  don't know I don't know I think I would  have taken the job just to make money to  to do this you know I love doing it so  much and so I knew I had to continue I  had no idea what the form would look  like I had no idea what built this  popular website that eventually be on  YouTube I had no idea any of that was  gonna happen I just knew that I had to  continue it and I think that's when you  have that moment it's a very exciting  but also dangerous time because if you  think too logically if I thought just  with my head I wouldn't have continued  right I wouldn't have made sense  logically it doesn't make sense to do  this if I talk to people about it and  they looked at you know the stats and  the market research it wouldn't have  made any sense like what you're doing  you can't you can't make money from this  entrepreneurs don't have money and even  if they did you only got three people to  a free event like it didn't make any  sense and that's where for a lot of  entrepreneurs their ideas die and they  they side with everybody else this yeah  you know what you're probably right that  was a stupid idea I should have done  that where there's still something like  hey you know what maybe there was a way  to make it work you know you kind of you  feel like there's something that could  have could have worked out and so I  didn't give up on my idea even though I  had no idea how it would work out and  because you often don't have all the  answers at the beginning you start to  doubt yourself and I guess don't doubt  yourself right and and it's okay not  having all the answers yet and it's okay  that you're gonna struggle and it's okay  that nobody comes to your event and it's  okay that you're not making money yet  you don't have the answers yet you're  working on it but you you will figure it  out if you keep going and you keep  following your passion you will figure  it out it's going to take longer than  you want it to take it might cost more  money than you want it to take you know  we're inpatient we want things now but  it will work out if you keep following  your passion so that's my story that's  kind of my unique I guess Eureka moment  and thank you for asking the question so  for those you watching you like the  video please give a thumbs up below if  you have a question for me or if you  want to share your Eureka moment please  leave it in the comment section below  I love seeing those come in they really  make my day every time they do and if  you want to see more videos like this  you can click on my face up there and  subscribe to this channel thank you so  much and I'll see you soon
 

